[b][size=5]Make Solasta co-op smoother.[/size][/b]

Shared interactions, automatic confirmations, teammate visibility and configurable movement speed. Open [b]F8[/b] to configure the mod.

[b]Version 0.1.27[/b], Fixes the missing lobby swap controls, reduces the automatic-move replacement cooldown to 0.25 seconds and reduces repeated exploration scans. Swap buttons appear on the hero cards below the owner dropdown; no F8 setting is needed. Travel preview remains off by default, dialogue defaults to Follow host, exploration speed x1.75 and combat speed x1.5.

[b][size=4]CO-OP & EXPLORATION[/size][/b]

[b]Lobby Party Order[/b], Once all heroes are selected, the host clicks Move slot N on one character card, below the owner dropdown, then Swap with M on another. No F8 setting is needed. Clicking the selected slot cancels. Guests see the same order; new and loaded games use it through native party sorting. Each hero stays under the same player's control, and later manual in-game ordering remains available.
[b]Shared Travel[/b], View the host's travel screen and player cursors. The preview is off by default; press F6 to enable it.
[b]Shared Loot[/b], Access chests, corpses and ground loot together.
[b]Auto-Follow[/b], Follow teammates and their movement destinations, including new host targets during an automatic walk. Manual movement and interactions remain protected; following resumes after pauses.
[b]Auto-Confirmations[/b], Accept fast-travel votes and continue ready loading screens.
[b]Item Transfers[/b], Increase the distance for transferring items.

[b][size=4]SPEED, LOOT & DIALOGUE[/size][/b]

[b]Combat Speed[/b], Speed up actual movement across the battlefield, movement waits, animations and VFX.
[b]Exploration Speed[/b], A separate movement slider for exploring locations. Both sliders cover [b]x1 to x3[/b], with 0.25 steps and x1/x2/x3 presets. Default combat speed x1.5, exploration speed x1.75. Cinematic movement keeps native timing.
[b]Empty Loot[/b], Automatically close chest, corpse and ground-loot windows after all items have been taken and pending transfers have completed.
[b]Empty Container Highlights[/b], Hide highlights on already opened empty containers. Unopened containers remain visible and interaction remains available.
[b]Dialogue Votes[/b], Choose Vanilla, Follow host (default), or Random tie. Follow host needs no guest click. Random tie counts all players equally and chooses once on the host when tied, giving two different votes a [b]50/50 chance[/b].
[b]Dialogue Autosave[/b], Save before dialogue interactions and scripted trigger acknowledgement when native saving is allowed. The game cannot separately restore a choice or roll inside an active dialogue; scenes that forbid saving are skipped.

The host controls speed and dialogue policy for the room. Guests use the same settings and vote result. Preferences are remembered between launches. Empty-loot options are configurable per player.

[b][size=4]INTERFACE & UTILITIES[/size][/b]

[b]Teammate Panels[/b], View teammate actions, spells and abilities in native read-only panels.
[b]Detailed Tooltips[/b], Extended descriptions without holding Alt.
[b]Targeting Range[/b], Display spell and attack distances.
[b]Camera Zoom[/b], Extend the maximum zoom-out distance, default x1.4.
[b]Connection Settings[/b], Photon TCP transport and guarded room-join retries.
[b]Diagnostics[/b], Verbose logging and diagnostic reports.

[b][size=4]INSTALLATION[/size][/b]

1. Close Solasta on every computer.
2. Download the latest ZIP from the Files tab and extract [b]winhttp.dll[/b].
3. Copy [b]winhttp.dll[/b] into the game folder, next to [b]Solasta.exe[/b].
4. Launch the game and open [b]F8[/b].

[b]All co-op players must use the same mod version.[/b]

[b][size=4]HOTKEYS[/size][/b]

[b]F6[/b], Shared travel preview
[b]F7[/b], Targeting range
[b]F8[/b], Mod settings
[b]F9[/b], Verbose logging
[b]F10[/b], Diagnostic report

Windows x64. Manual installation, no Unity Mod Manager required. Other mods using winhttp.dll may conflict. This is an unofficial community mod, not affiliated with Tactical Adventures.

